  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In the Wang tribe pitch, Bei Cao Sheng places Lord Pei Yan Fei beside Bei tribe’s forest soldier corps and Zheng tribe’s lightning spear formation as the ally who can bypass troops and kill an enslavement path leader, and he states Pei Yan Fei has already reached rank four peak stage.",
      "chapters": [
        478
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_wang_tribe",
        "char_bei_cao_sheng",
        "fac_bei_tribe",
        "fac_zheng_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Ge tribe elder later warns of the same rank four peak stage fame when the three tribe alliance gathers against Ge tribe near crescent lake.",
      "chapters": [
        479
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ge_tribe",
        "loc_crescent_lake"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is eight feet tall. His eyes are sharp and full of power. His back is wide and his waist is thin. His black eyebrows shine with a dark luster. They are thick in the middle and sharp at both ends, with the tip raised slightly, like a swallow’s wings. The eyebrows are the imprint of two rank four swallow wings Gu. Another pair of swallow wings can grow from his back.",
      "chapters": [
        482
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On that field he is Pei tribe leader: eight feet tall, broad back and thin waist, with black eyebrows that are the imprint of two rank four Swallow Wings Gu. He is a metal path Gu Master with sharp attacks and strong low altitude flight short of master level, and he kills Ge tribe elders in the wolf group rather than locking onto Fang Yuan, forcing one myriad wolf king to stay on guard. When the wall breaks he returns with golden coat Gu, a second pair of swallow wings, and rainbow transformation Gu to form the killer move Golden Rainbow Strike, which pierces turtleback myriad wolf king through its shell and leaves him pale in the air. Fang Yuan’s five hundred year memories already know he holds rank five Do or Die Gu, which can refill primeval essence at the cost of a cultivation stage drop.",
      "chapters": [
        482
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "night-fight-at-pei-tribe-camp",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_pei_tribe",
        "gu_swallow_wings_gu",
        "sys_gu_master",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "move_golden_rainbow_strike",
        "gu_do_or_die_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He refuses Bei Cao Chuan’s call to chase while Pei tribe is bait, then activates Do or Die Gu, fills his aperture, and charges Chang Shan Yin until a white-eyes wolf stands with the remaining myriad kings and he stops rather than risk Pei tribe again.",
      "chapters": [
        483
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "do-or-die-gu-and-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bei_cao_chuan",
        "char_chang_shan_yin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later report among nearby tribes states that Ge tribe’s night challenge left him, a fierce general in northern plains, down a small realm of cultivation.",
      "chapters": [
        484
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "do-or-die-gu-and-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Liu Wen Wu sends him against Hao Ji Liu at rank four upper stage on both sides; he uses Golden Rainbow Strike again, is fooled by water image Gu, and flees on swallow wings.",
      "chapters": [
        525
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "liu-tribe-and-hei-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_liu_wen_wu",
        "char_hao_ji_liu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Liu Wen Wu loses, he attaches to Hei tribe but still cannot take Hao Ji Liu’s place as first general.",
      "chapters": [
        537
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "liu-tribe-and-hei-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hei_tribe"
      ]
    }
  ],
